\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 Query Sculpting\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Query Sculpting was introduced by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ppc-epiphany.com/2014/12/08/taking-google-shopping-to-the-next-level/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Martin Roettgerding}} that structures the account into three campaigns:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Product Campaign\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Brand Campaign\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Others Campaign\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Negative keywords and campaign priority settings are used to filter search queries into the appropriate campaign.\
Brand names are added as negative keywords in the highest priority campaign to ensure brand searches show listings from the Brand Campaign.\
The advantages are that you can analyze query performance separately and set bids accordingly for each campaign type.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
